# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VAPT Verification Orchestrator — repository safety .gitignore
#
# The rules in this file exist to PREVENT real client data, private engagement
# profiles, credentials and imported scanner output from ever being committed.
# Do not relax these rules without reviewing docs/SECURITY.md. The automated
# client-data safety checker (`vapt-verify security scan`) also enforces this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Private engagement profiles (real client data lives here, local only) ---
# Ignore ALL contents but keep the directory via .gitkeep. The `/*` form (not
# `profiles/private/`) is required so the .gitkeep negation can take effect.
profiles/private/*
!profiles/private/.gitkeep

# --- Real scanner exports must never be committed ---
# Synthetic test fixtures live under tests/fixtures/ and are the ONLY .nessus
# files permitted in the repository; they are force-added explicitly there.
*.nessus
*.nessus.xml
!tests/fixtures/**/*.nessus

# Other raw scanner exports
*.csv
!tests/fixtures/**/*.csv
!profiles/examples/**/*.csv
*.qualys.xml
*.openvas.xml

# --- Generated engagement workspaces / evidence bundles ---
engagements/*
!engagements/.gitkeep
evidence/
reports/local/

# --- Credentials & secrets ---
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
.env
.env.*
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.secret

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.env/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
